{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KUSFuW59RWuFavChgUJN9G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each planned experiment in the experiment plan, under the \"best\" tier scenario. I need to provide specific metric predictions with rationales for why those results would occur in this best-case scenario.\n\nLet me carefully go through each experiment and generate realistic \"best\" tier predictions based on the defined key metrics ranges and narrative direction.\n\nKey metrics ranges for \"best\" tier:\n- formality_pairwise_winrate_per_judge: [0.6, 0.75]\n\n\n- formality_sign_test_p_per_judge: [0.001, 0.05]\n- cross_benchmark_significant_combos: [5, 9]\n- tone_nli_pass_rate: [0.85, 0.93]\n- tone_pairwise_winrate: [0.58, 0.7]\n- tone_pairwise_p: [0.001, 0.05]\n- likert_pairwise_gap_prevalence: [0.67, 1.0]\n- original_preference_winrate_exp005: [0.47, 0.53]\n- direction_asymmetry_max\n\n_gap: [0.05, 0.15]\n- scaled_n500_formal_winrate: [0.6, 0.72]\n\nLooking at the baseline results from the pairwise comparison between Claude-3.5 and GPT-4o on LLMBar, I see formal language achieves about 69% win rate with strong statistical significance. Now I'm setting up predictions for the planned experiments, starting with multi-judge formality evaluation across different model pairs and benchmarks.\n\nFor the first experiment with Claude and Gemini judges, I expect formality bias to hold up across different models, though Claude's tendency toward better calibration might produce slightly lower effect sizes than GPT-4o while still remaining statistically significant.\n\nFor the second experiment, I need to verify the effect generalizes across different benchmarks—AlpacaEval and MT-Bench have different response characteristics, so the magnitude might shift even if the pattern persists. I'm aiming for at least 5-8 additional significant combinations beyond the one we already have.\n\nFor the third experiment, I'm testing whether Likert scales consistently fail to capture what pairwise comparisons detect.\n\nThe tone axis is the second dimension to explore, with similar success criteria around win rates and statistical significance. I'm also checking whether the original preference distribution stays near 50-50, confirming that style drives the effect rather than inherent model preference. At scale with n=500, the win rates should tighten and the confidence intervals should narrow. The register axis should show a similar but potentially weaker effect, and I need to test whether non-Qwen rewriters produce comparable results as a control.\n\nNow I'm organizing all these experiments into a structured format.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11418,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11418},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"716ef52e-c7c5-4277-86fe-b34ea8047dee","uuid":"de866b70-b6fd-4f3e-9170-c77bde7e11a0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KUSFuW59RWuFavChgUJN9G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 framing 完全成立。CSD 作为通用 black-box causal style bias detection framework，\n  在 3 judges × 3 benchmarks × 2+ axes 上系统验证。Formality bias 跨 judge/benchmark 稳定复现，\n  tone axis 成功开辟第二维度，C2 Likert-Pairwise gap 系统性存在，original preference 可忽略。\n  Verbosity failure 作为 principled method boundary 增强方法论严谨性。\n  Paper 叙事：problem → method → systematic evidence → measurement gap revelation → method boundary analysis。\n  EMNLP Main 三条 claims 全部成立，Main conference 竞争力充足。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet、Claude-4-Sonnet、Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用 MVP 阶段已生成的 counterfactual pairs（n=100），每个 judge 做 dual-direction pairwise，\n      position control。与 GPT-4o baseline (69.1%, p=0.006) 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate: 0.64\n      claude_sonnet_sign_test_p: 0.028\n      claude_sonnet_n_consistent: 50\n      claude_sonnet_formal_wins: 32\n      claude_sonnet_casual_wins: 18\n      gemini_flash_formal_win_rate: 0.72\n      gemini_flash_sign_test_p: 0.002\n      gemini_flash_n_consistent: 58\n      gemini_flash_formal_wins: 42\n      gemini_flash_casual_wins: 16\n      judges_significant_count: 3\n      judges_total: 3\n      cross_judge_winrate_range: [0.64, 0.72]\n      cross_judge_mean_winrate: 0.684\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality bias 是 LLM judge 的通用现象而非 GPT-4o 特有，因为 RLHF 训练数据普遍偏向\n      formal/professional 风格的回答——这是 preference data 的系统性采样偏差。Claude-Sonnet 效应\n      略弱（0.64 vs GPT-4o 0.69），因为 Anthropic 的 RLHF 流程有更多 helpfulness 导向的校准，\n      对 surface style 的依赖稍低；但 formal premium 仍然显著，因为底层 pretraining 数据中\n      formal text 与 higher-quality content 高度相关。Gemini-Flash 效应略强（0.72），因为\n      轻量模型更依赖 surface heuristics（style proxy）来做判断，formal tone 作为 quality\n      shortcut 的权重更大。三个 judge 全部显著（p<0.05）支持 A1 假设。效应量级差异\n      （0.64-0.72）同时支持 C3——bias 的 magnitude 是 judge-dependent 的。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: Formality Pairwise Results Across Judges (LLMBar, n=100)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal Wins\", \"Casual Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"95% CI\", \"Sign Test p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 55, 38, 17, \"69.1%\", \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\", \"0.006**\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 50, 32, 18, \"64.0%\", \"[50.1%, 75.9%]\", \"0.028*\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 58, 42, 16, \"72.4%\", \"[59.8%, 82.3%]\", \"0.002**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: 三个 judge 的 formal win rate 森林图（forest plot），每个 judge 一行，显示 point estimate + 95% Wilson CI。所有三个 CI 不跨 0.5 baseline，视觉上清晰展示 formality premium 的 cross-judge 一致性。\"\n      - \"Figure 3: Direction asymmetry grouped bar chart——每个 judge 分 formal→casual orig 和 casual→formal orig 两组，展示 win rate 差异。GPT-4o 不对称最大（~0.24 gap），Claude 最小（~0.10 gap）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      三个 judge 全部显著复现 formality bias，A1 假设成立。效应量级在 0.64-0.72 范围内，\n      跨 judge 一致但有量级差异——这是 C3（axis-dependency）的 judge 维度证据。\n      Gemini-Flash 最强可能反映轻量模型对 surface cues 更敏感。\n      方向不对称在所有 judge 上存在但程度不同：GPT-4o 最大（formal←casual orig 方向更强），\n      Claude 最对称——这为 exp-005 original preference 控制提供了动机。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 CSD 流程。需要新的 counterfactual generation\n      （不同 source text）。三个 judge（GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash）分别评测。\n      每个 benchmark n=100。与 LLMBar 结果交叉比较，形成 3×3 矩阵。\n    expected_results:\n      # AlpacaEval results\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.67\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_p: 0.012\n      alpacaeval_claude_formal_winrate: 0.61\n      alpacaeval_claude_p: 0.048\n      alpacaeval_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.70\n      alpacaeval_gemini_p: 0.004\n      alpacaeval_counterfactual_nli_pass: 0.90\n      # MT-Bench results\n      mtbench_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.65\n      mtbench_gpt4o_p: 0.018\n      mtbench_claude_formal_winrate: 0.60\n      mtbench_claude_p: 0.065\n      mtbench_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.68\n      mtbench_gemini_p: 0.008\n      mtbench_counterfactual_nli_pass: 0.87\n      # Cross-benchmark summary\n      significant_combos_total: 7\n      total_combos: 9\n      non_significant_combos: [\"Claude×MT-Bench (p=0.065)\",\"(borderline)\"]\n      mean_winrate_across_all: 0.668\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality bias 跨 benchmark 泛化，因为 bias 源于 judge 的内在偏好而非特定数据集的特征。\n      AlpacaEval 效应略强于 MT-Bench：AlpacaEval 的 open-ended instruction-following 任务\n      给 style variation 更大空间，formal tone 作为 quality proxy 的作用更明显；MT-Bench\n      的 multi-turn 结构和更 specific 的评判标准（如 math/reasoning accuracy）部分抑制了\n      style 的影响。Claude×MT-Bench 是唯一 borderline 不显著的组合（p=0.065），因为\n      Claude 在 MT-Bench 这种有明确正确性标准的 benchmark 上更倾向 content-based 判断。\n      但 7/9 组合显著（含 LLMBar 数据）远超偶然水平，A2 假设成立。\n      NLI pass rate 在 AlpacaEval (0.90) 略高于 MT-Bench (0.87)，因为 AlpacaEval 的\n      response 结构更简单，counterfactual 改写更容易保持语义。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: Formality Pairwise Win Rate Matrix (Judge × Benchmark)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"LLMBar\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"MT-Bench\", \"Mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"69.1%**\", \"67.0%*\", \"65.0%*\", \"67.0%\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", \"64.0%*\", \"61.0%*\", \"60.0%†\", \"61.7%\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", \"72.4%**\", \"70.0%**\", \"68.0%**\", \"70.1%\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"68.5%\", \"66.0%\", \"64.3%\", \"66.3%\"]\n        footnote: \"** p<0.01, * p<0.05, † p<0.10. n=100 per cell (n_consistent varies).\"\n      - title: \"Table 4: Counterfactual Quality per Benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"n\", \"NLI Pass Rate\", \"NLI Mean\", \"BERTScore Mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", 100, \"88%\", 0.896, 0.842]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", 100, \"90%\", 0.908, 0.851]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", 100, \"87%\", 0.882, 0.835]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 4: 3×3 heatmap，行为 judge，列为 benchmark，颜色深度表示 formal win rate（0.5-0.8 色标），每格标注 win rate 和显著性星号。视觉上一目了然：整个矩阵偏暖色，Gemini 行最深，MT-Bench 列最浅。\"\n      - \"Figure 5: Benchmark 间 effect size 比较——三个 benchmark 的 win rate 分布 boxplot，展示 LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench 的梯度。\"\n    analysis: >\n      9 个 judge×benchmark 组合中 7 个显著（p<0.05），剩余 1 个 borderline（Claude×MT-Bench p=0.065），\n      仅 0 个完全不显著。这远超 A2 要求的 5-9 个显著组合的下限。\n      Benchmark 梯度（LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench）有方法论意义：task-specific evaluation criteria\n      越强，style bias 越被抑制——这为 \"style bias 在 open-ended evaluation 中危害最大\" 的论点提供证据。\n      Judge 梯度（Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude）稳定跨 benchmark，说明 judge 的 style sensitivity\n      是其内在属性。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对 exp-001 和 exp-002 的每个 judge×benchmark 组合，计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate，\n      系统性比较两种 measurement 的 sensitivity。使用同一 counterfactual 数据。\n    expected_results:\n      # LLMBar\n      llmbar_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.10\n      llmbar_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.332\n      llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_winrate: 0.691\n      llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      llmbar_gpt4o_gap: true\n      llmbar_claude_likert_ate: 0.06\n      llmbar_claude_likert_p: 0.485\n      llmbar_claude_pairwise_winrate: 0.640\n      llmbar_claude_pairwise_p: 0.028\n      llmbar_claude_gap: true\n      llmbar_gemini_likert_ate: 0.14\n      llmbar_gemini_likert_p: 0.198\n      llmbar_gemini_pairwise_winrate: 0.724\n      llmbar_gemini_pairwise_p: 0.002\n      llmbar_gemini_gap: true\n      # AlpacaEval\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.08\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.412\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_pairwise_p: 0.012\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_gap: true\n      alpacaeval_claude_likert_p: 0.551\n      alpacaeval_claude_pairwise_p: 0.048\n      alpacaeval_claude_gap: true\n      alpacaeval_gemini_likert_p: 0.142\n      alpacaeval_gemini_pairwise_p: 0.004\n      alpacaeval_gemini_gap: true\n      # MT-Bench\n      mtbench_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.388\n      mtbench_gpt4o_pairwise_p: 0.018\n      mtbench_gpt4o_gap: true\n      mtbench_claude_likert_p: 0.612\n      mtbench_claude_pairwise_p: 0.065\n      mtbench_claude_gap: false\n      mtbench_gemini_likert_p: 0.175\n      mtbench_gemini_pairwise_p: 0.008\n      mtbench_gemini_gap: true\n      # Summary\n      gap_prevalence: 0.78\n      combos_with_gap: 7\n      combos_without_gap: 2\n      combos_total: 9\n      note: \"两个无 gap 的组合：Claude×MT-Bench（两者都不显著），因此不算 gap（一致性 non-significant）\"\n      mean_likert_p: 0.37\n      mean_pairwise_p: 0.021\n    result_rationale: >\n      Likert-Pairwise gap 的根因是 measurement scale 的信息结构差异。Likert pointwise 评分中，\n      style bias 被 (1) score anchoring（judge 倾向使用量表中段）、(2) absolute calibration noise\n      （不同 item 的 baseline quality 不同）、(3) within-subject variance 稀释。Pairwise 直接\n      呈现 A/B 对比，消除了 absolute calibration 问题，将 style 差异放大为 forced choice 中的\n      tie-breaking signal。在 best 档位，7/9 组合出现 gap（Likert 不显著但 Pairwise 显著），\n      gap prevalence 0.78 在 [0.67, 1.0] 范围内。唯一无 gap 的是 Claude×MT-Bench（两者都\n      不显著——pairwise 也仅 borderline p=0.065），这不违反 C2 因为 C2 的 claim 是 Likert\n      \"低估\" 而非 \"永远 miss\"：当 pairwise 也 miss 时，说明该组合的 true effect 本身很弱。\n      没有任何组合出现 Likert 显著但 Pairwise 不显著的 reverse pattern，强力支持 pairwise\n      严格更敏感的结论。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate — Systematic Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Judge × Benchmark\", \"Likert ATE\", \"Likert p\", \"Pairwise WR\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Gap?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar\", \"+0.10\", \"0.332\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar\", \"+0.06\", \"0.485\", \"64.0%\", \"0.028*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar\", \"+0.14\", \"0.198\", \"72.4%\", \"0.002**\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.08\", \"0.412\", \"67.0%\", \"0.012*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Claude × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.04\", \"0.551\", \"61.0%\", \"0.048*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.12\", \"0.142\", \"70.0%\", \"0.004**\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × MT-Bench\", \"+0.09\", \"0.388\", \"65.0%\", \"0.018*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Claude × MT-Bench\", \"+0.03\", \"0.612\", \"60.0%\", \"0.065†\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × MT-Bench\", \"+0.11\", \"0.175\", \"68.0%\", \"0.008**\", \"✓\"]\n        footnote: \"Gap = Likert p>0.10 AND Pairwise p<0.05. † borderline.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 6 (论文核心图): Paired dot plot——每个 judge×benchmark 组合一对点（Likert p 和 Pairwise p），用线段连接。Horizontal line 标注 α=0.05。几乎所有 Likert 点在线上方，Pairwise 点在线下方，视觉冲击力极强，直观展示 measurement gap。\"\n      - \"Figure 7: Likert score 分布 violin plot（formal vs casual），展示 why Likert fails——分布高度重叠，mean difference 被 variance 淹没。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 是本文最强 contribution。7/9 组合出现系统性 measurement gap，且无 reverse pattern。\n      这意味着现有文献中使用 Likert pointwise 方法研究 style bias 的工作（如基于 Likert 的\n      debiasing）可能系统性低估问题的严重程度。实践建议明确：style bias audit 应使用\n      pairwise comparison 而非 pointwise scoring。这个 insight 对 LLM-as-judge 社区\n      有直接、广泛的实用价值——是最强 reviewer hook。\n\n  - name: \"Tone axis (assertive/hedging) counterfactual + pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      测试 tone（assertive vs hedging）作为第二个工作维度。Full pipeline：counterfactual\n      generation → NLI content verification → pairwise scoring（dual-direction）→ ATE 分析。\n      三个 judge（GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash）× LLMBar。n=100。\n    expected_results:\n      # Content verification\n      tone_nli_pass_rate: 0.89\n      tone_nli_mean: 0.912\n      tone_bertscore_mean: 0.858\n      tone_both_pass: 0.86\n      # GPT-4o pairwise\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 52\n      gpt4o_assertive_wins: 33\n      gpt4o_hedging_wins: 19\n      gpt4o_assertive_win_rate: 0.635\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.038\n      # Claude pairwise\n      claude_n_consistent: 48\n      claude_assertive_wins: 28\n      claude_hedging_wins: 20\n      claude_assertive_win_rate: 0.583\n      claude_sign_test_p: 0.085\n      # Gemini pairwise\n      gemini_n_consistent: 54\n      gemini_assertive_wins: 37\n      gemini_hedging_wins: 17\n      gemini_assertive_win_rate: 0.685\n      gemini_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      # Cross-judge summary\n      judges_significant: 2\n      judges_total: 3\n      mean_assertive_winrate: 0.634\n      # Likert comparison (for C2)\n      gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.07\n      gpt4o_likert_p: 0.448\n      claude_likert_p: 0.621\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.231\n      tone_likert_pairwise_gap: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Tone axis 成功开辟第二维度，因为 assertive/hedging 改写在语义保持上与 formality 类似——\n      改变表达的确信程度（confidence markers, hedging phrases）而不改变信息内容，NLI pass 0.89\n      在 [0.85, 0.93] 范围内。Assertive tone 产生 premium 的机制与 formality 平行但不同：\n      LLM judge 在 RLHF 中学到 \"confident = competent\" 的 heuristic，assertive 回答被\n      associative 地认为更 knowledgeable。效应略弱于 formality（mean 0.634 vs 0.684），\n      因为 tone 是更微妙的 surface cue——formality 涉及词汇和句法层面的系统性变化，\n      而 tone 主要体现在 hedging markers 和 modal verbs 上，judge 的 sensitivity 更低。\n      Claude 在 tone 上 borderline 不显著（p=0.085），因为 Anthropic 训练中可能有更多\n      关于 epistemic humility 的 alignment，对 hedging 的 penalty 较小。Gemini 仍然最强\n      （0.685），进一步确认轻量模型对 surface cues 更 sensitive。两个 judge 显著 + 一个\n      borderline 足以支持 C1 和 C3 在 tone axis 上的 claim。A3 和 A4 假设成立。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 6: Tone Axis Content Verification\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"n\", 100]\n          - [\"NLI Pass Rate (≥0.85)\", \"89%\"]\n          - [\"NLI Mean\", 0.912]\n          - [\"BERTScore Mean\", 0.858]\n          - [\"Both Pass Rate\", \"86%\"]\n      - title: \"Table 7: Tone (Assertive vs Hedging) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Assert. Wins\", \"Hedge Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"95% CI\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 52, 33, 19, \"63.5%\", \"[49.9%, 75.2%]\", \"0.038*\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 48, 28, 20, \"58.3%\", \"[44.3%, 71.1%]\", \"0.085†\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 54, 37, 17, \"68.5%\", \"[55.4%, 79.3%]\", \"0.006**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 8: 双 axis 效应比较——grouped bar chart，x 轴为 judge，每个 judge 两根 bar（formality win rate 和 tone win rate），展示 axis-dependency。Formality bar 系统性高于 tone bar，但两者都在 50% 以上。\"\n      - \"Figure 9: Tone counterfactual 示例对比——展示 2-3 个 assertive/hedging pair，标注 NLI score，帮助读者理解改写质量。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Tone axis 成功验证 CSD 框架的 multi-axis 能力。两个 axis 效应模式不同\n      （formality 更强且跨 judge 一致，tone 略弱且 Claude 上 borderline），\n      直接支持 C3——style bias 是 axis-dependent 的，不能把 \"style\" 当单一维度。\n      Tone 的 Likert 同样全部不显著，进一步扩展 C2 的 evidence。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Original text vs 同风格 double-rewrite 的 pairwise 比较。量化 original preference\n      confound。如果 win rate ≈50%，original preference 可忽略，style 是主要驱动力。\n      GPT-4o × LLMBar，n=100。\n    expected_results:\n      n_valid: 95\n      n_consistent: 60\n      original_wins: 32\n      rewrite_wins: 28\n      original_win_rate: 0.533\n      sign_test_p: 0.362\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.408\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.655\n      position_bias_check: 0.52\n      # Subgroup analysis\n      formal_orig_original_winrate: 0.55\n      casual_orig_original_winrate: 0.52\n      nli_ge90_original_winrate: 0.51\n    result_rationale: >\n      Original preference 可忽略（win rate 0.533 在 [0.47, 0.53] 范围边缘，p=0.362 远不显著），\n      因为 double-rewrite 过程虽然引入了轻微的 \"rewrite artifact\"（如稍微不自然的措辞），\n      但这个 artifact 对 judge 的影响是随机的而非系统性的。Win rate 略偏向 original（53.3%\n      而非精确 50%），反映了 rewrite 过程确实有微小的 quality degradation，但量级远小于\n      formality 的 69.1% 或 tone 的 63.5%。这意味着 exp-001/002/004 中观察到的 style\n      premium 主要由 style 本身驱动，而非 \"original 比 rewrite 更自然\" 的 confound。\n      方向不对称（MVP 中 formal←casual orig 0.79 vs casual←formal orig 0.55）的主要解释\n      从 \"original preference\" 转向 \"改写方向的非对称难度\"：将 casual 改为 formal 更容易\n      保持质量，因此 formal←casual 方向的 counterfactual 质量更高，效应更强。\n      A6 假设成立：direction asymmetry 主要由 style 驱动，original preference 贡献 <5%。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 8: Original Preference Control (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"n (valid pairs)\", 95]\n          - [\"n (consistent)\", 60]\n          - [\"Original Wins\", 32]\n          - [\"Rewrite Wins\", 28]\n          - [\"Original Win Rate\", \"53.3%\"]\n          - [\"95% CI\", \"[40.8%, 65.5%]\"]\n          - [\"Sign Test p\", \"0.362\"]\n      - title: \"Table 9: Effect Size Decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"Win Rate\", \"p\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formality premium (CSD)\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"Style-driven causal effect\"]\n          - [\"Original preference\", \"53.3%\", \"0.362\", \"Negligible confound\"]\n          - [\"Corrected formality estimate\", \"~65.8%\", \"—\", \"Conservative lower bound\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 10: 三组 win rate 对比 bar chart——formality pairwise (69.1%), tone pairwise (63.5%), original preference control (53.3%)，各带 95% CI error bar。Original preference 的 CI 跨 50%，而 style axes 的 CI 不跨 50%。直观展示 style effect vs confound 的量级差异。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference confound 可安全忽略。53.3% 的微小偏移可解释 direction asymmetry\n      的一小部分（≤3-5 个百分点），但 formality 的 19.1% premium 和 tone 的 13.5% premium\n      远大于此。保守估计（扣除 original preference 后）formality 仍有 ~15.8% premium，\n      高度显著。这回应了 RC3 reviewer concern。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 formality pairwise 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=500。选择 exp-001/002 中效应最强的\n      judge×benchmark 组合（预期 Gemini×LLMBar）。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable\n      effect size。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 500\n      n_valid_both_trials: 490\n      n_consistent: 282\n      formal_wins: 192\n      casual_wins: 90\n      formal_win_rate: 0.681\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.624\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.733\n      sign_test_p: 0.0000003\n      cohens_h: 0.378\n      # Power analysis\n      power_at_n100_for_d065: 0.72\n      power_at_n300_for_d065: 0.97\n      power_at_n500_for_d065: 0.995\n      minimum_detectable_effect_n500: 0.56\n      # Subgroup stability\n      first_100_winrate: 0.70\n      second_100_winrate: 0.67\n      third_100_winrate: 0.69\n      fourth_100_winrate: 0.66\n      fifth_100_winrate: 0.70\n      subgroup_variance: 0.0003\n      # NLI stratification at scale\n      nli_ge90_n: 420\n      nli_ge90_winrate: 0.695\n      nli_ge80_n: 465\n      nli_ge80_winrate: 0.683\n    result_rationale: >\n      Scaled replication 在 n=500 时 win rate 0.681 在 [0.6, 0.72] 范围内，与 n=100\n      的 0.691 高度一致（仅 -1% regression to mean），说明 MVP 阶段的 point estimate\n      不是 small-sample 侥幸。CI 从 n=100 的 [0.56, 0.80] 收窄到 [0.62, 0.73]，\n      p 值从 0.006 降到 <0.001，sign_test_p 达到 3×10⁻⁷ 量级。五个 n=100 子组的\n      win rate 在 0.66-0.70 范围内波动极小（σ²=0.0003），展示效应的高度稳定性。\n      Power analysis 显示 n=100 对 d=0.065（Likert ATE 量级）只有 0.72 power——\n      这正好解释了为什么 Likert 在 n=100 时 miss：不是 Likert 完全无效，而是对弱信号\n      的 statistical power 不足。n=500 时 power 达 0.995，即使 Likert 也应 borderline\n      显著——但 pairwise 在 n=100 就能 catch，说明 pairwise 的 effective sample size\n      更大（每对 within-subject 对比消除了 item-level variance）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 10: Scaled Replication — Formality Pairwise (Gemini × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Scale\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal WR\", \"95% CI\", \"p\", \"Cohen's h\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"n=100 (MVP)\", 55, \"69.1%\", \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\", \"0.006\", \"0.393\"]\n          - [\"n=100 (sub1)\", 58, \"70.0%\", \"[57.3%, 80.4%]\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"n=100 (sub2)\", 54, \"67.0%\", \"[53.7%, 78.1%]\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"n=100 (sub3)\", 56, \"69.0%\", \"[56.1%, 79.6%]\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"n=100 (sub4)\", 55, \"66.0%\", \"[52.9%, 77.1%]\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"n=100 (sub5)\", 59, \"70.0%\", \"[57.5%, 80.2%]\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"n=500 (full)\", 282, \"68.1%\", \"[62.4%, 73.3%]\", \"<0.001\", \"0.378\"]\n      - title: \"Table 11: Power Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"n\", \"Power (d=0.065)\", \"Power (d=0.18)\", \"Min Detectable WR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [100, \"0.72\", \"0.99\", \"62.0%\"]\n          - [300, \"0.97\", \">0.999\", \"57.5%\"]\n          - [500, \"0.995\", \">0.999\", \"56.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 11: Cumulative win rate plot——x 轴为 sample size (50→500)，y 轴为 cumulative formal win rate，带 running 95% CI band。Win rate 从早期波动逐渐收敛到 ~0.68，CI band 稳定收窄。\"\n      - \"Figure 12: Power curve——x 轴为 n，y 轴为 power，三条线分别对应 d=0.065 (Likert ATE), d=0.18 (pairwise effect), d=0.10 (intermediate)。标注 n=100 和 n=500 的 power 值。直观展示 Likert 在 n=100 power 不足的原因。\"\n    analysis: >\n      n=500 replication 是对 RC5 (sample size) 的决定性回应。效应稳定、CI 收窄、\n      p 值极小。Power analysis 同时为 C2 提供了额外解释——Likert 的 measurement gap\n      部分来自 power 不足（pointwise 的 between-item variance 稀释了 weak signal），\n      而 pairwise 的 within-subject design 在 n=100 就有足够 power。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      第三个 surface-level axis。Academic vs conversational register 改变词汇和句法\n      但不改变信息内容。Full pipeline：counterfactual gen → content verification →\n      pairwise scoring。三个 judge × LLMBar，n=100。\n    expected_results:\n      # Content verification\n      register_nli_pass_rate: 0.86\n      register_nli_mean: 0.893\n      register_bertscore_mean: 0.839\n      # Pairwise results\n      gpt4o_academic_win_rate: 0.66\n      gpt4o_p: 0.015\n      claude_academic_win_rate: 0.62\n      claude_p: 0.042\n      gemini_academic_win_rate: 0.71\n      gemini_p: 0.003\n      judges_significant: 3\n      mean_academic_winrate: 0.663\n      # Likert gap\n      gpt4o_likert_p: 0.289\n      claude_likert_p: 0.511\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.167\n      register_likert_pairwise_gap: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Register axis 效应在 formality 和 tone 之间（mean 0.663），因为 academic/conversational\n      register 的改变涉及词汇层面（Latinate vs Germanic words, disciplinary jargon vs\n      everyday terms）和句法层面（复杂从句 vs 简单句），比 tone 更 salient 但比 formality\n      更窄（formality 包含 register + tone + other cues 的 composite）。NLI pass rate 0.86\n      略低于 formality (0.88) 和 tone (0.89)，因为 academic register 中的 disciplinary\n      vocabulary 有时会引入微妙的语义偏移（如用术语替代 layman terms 可能 shift specificity），\n      但仍在 [0.85, 0.93] 范围内。三个 judge 全部显著，进一步证明 CSD 框架的通用性。\n      现在有 3 working axes + 1 failing axis (verbosity)，C3 的 evidence 非常充分。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 12: Register (Academic vs Conversational) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Academic Wins\", \"Conversational Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 53, 35, 18, \"66.0%\", \"0.015*\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 50, 31, 19, \"62.0%\", \"0.042*\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 56, 40, 16, \"71.4%\", \"0.003**\"]\n      - title: \"Table 13: Cross-Axis Summary (all on LLMBar, 3 judges)\"\n        columns: [\"Axis\", \"Mean WR\", \"Judges Sig.\", \"NLI Pass\", \"Likert Detects?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formality\", \"68.4%\", \"3/3\", \"88%\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"Register\", \"66.3%\", \"3/3\", \"86%\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"Tone\", \"63.4%\", \"2/3\", \"89%\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"Verbosity\", \"—\", \"—\", \"65%\", \"N/A (failed H1)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 13: 四 axis 汇总——每个 axis 一行 forest plot，formal/register/tone 都有显著 CI 不跨 0.5，verbosity 标注为 method boundary (NLI fail)。一图讲完整个 C3 story。\"\n    analysis: >\n      三个 working axes 构成强有力的 C3 evidence：style bias 是 axis-dependent 的，\n      且效应量级系统性排序（formality > register > tone）。这不是偶然——效应强度与\n      改写涉及的 linguistic level 数量正相关（formality 跨词汇+句法+语用，register 跨词汇+句法，\n      tone 主要在语用层）。Verbosity 作为第四个 axis 的失败提供了 principled boundary：\n      改变信息量的 axis 违反内容保持假设，是方法论限制而非方法失败。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为替代 rewriter，对 LLMBar formality 运行完整 pipeline。\n      与 Qwen3-32B 结果比较，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n    expected_results:\n      # Content verification comparison\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      llama_nli_mean: 0.881\n      llama_bertscore_mean: 0.836\n      qwen_nli_pass_rate: 0.88\n      qwen_nli_mean: 0.896\n      # Pairwise comparison (GPT-4o judge)\n      llama_formal_win_rate: 0.66\n      llama_sign_test_p: 0.015\n      qwen_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n      qwen_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      # Statistical comparison\n      winrate_difference: 0.031\n      fisher_exact_p_difference: 0.42\n      rewriter_effect_significant: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama rewriter 产生略低但仍显著的 formality premium（0.66 vs Qwen 0.69），\n      差异不显著（Fisher p=0.42）。Llama NLI pass rate 略低（0.85 vs 0.88），\n      因为 Llama-70B 在 instruction following 上略弱于 Qwen3-32B（后者受益于 Qwen3\n      的强 instruction tuning），导致少量 counterfactual 有轻微语义偏移。但关键结论\n      不变：formality bias 的检测不依赖于特定 rewriter family。3% 的 win rate 差异\n      在统计噪声范围内，可能反映 counterfactual quality 的微小差异而非系统性 artifact。\n      这排除了 \"Qwen rewriter 引入了某种被 judge 偏好的 writing pattern\" 的 confound。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 14: Rewriter Ablation (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality)\"\n        columns: [\"Rewriter\", \"NLI Pass\", \"NLI Mean\", \"Formal WR\", \"p\", \"n_consistent\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"88%\", 0.896, \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", 55]\n          - [\"Llama-3.1-70B\", \"85%\", 0.881, \"66.0%\", \"0.015*\", 52]\n          - [\"Difference\", \"-3%\", \"-0.015\", \"-3.1%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Fisher exact (diff)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"p=0.42\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure A1 (appendix): Side-by-side counterfactual 质量对比——Qwen vs Llama 的 NLI score 分布 histogram，分布形状相似，Llama 略左偏。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter ablation 确认 CSD 结果的 robustness。这是 appendix 级实验而非 main text，\n      但对 reviewer 质疑 rewriter choice 时提供决定性回应。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11418,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11418},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"716ef52e-c7c5-4277-86fe-b34ea8047dee","uuid":"bdfb2376-e1fe-4b35-850f-b2b89524dbc5"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":246071,"duration_api_ms":247895,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 framing 完全成立。CSD 作为通用 black-box causal style bias detection framework，\n  在 3 judges × 3 benchmarks × 2+ axes 上系统验证。Formality bias 跨 judge/benchmark 稳定复现，\n  tone axis 成功开辟第二维度，C2 Likert-Pairwise gap 系统性存在，original preference 可忽略。\n  Verbosity failure 作为 principled method boundary 增强方法论严谨性。\n  Paper 叙事：problem → method → systematic evidence → measurement gap revelation → method boundary analysis。\n  EMNLP Main 三条 claims 全部成立，Main conference 竞争力充足。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet、Claude-4-Sonnet、Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用 MVP 阶段已生成的 counterfactual pairs（n=100），每个 judge 做 dual-direction pairwise，\n      position control。与 GPT-4o baseline (69.1%, p=0.006) 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate: 0.64\n      claude_sonnet_sign_test_p: 0.028\n      claude_sonnet_n_consistent: 50\n      claude_sonnet_formal_wins: 32\n      claude_sonnet_casual_wins: 18\n      gemini_flash_formal_win_rate: 0.72\n      gemini_flash_sign_test_p: 0.002\n      gemini_flash_n_consistent: 58\n      gemini_flash_formal_wins: 42\n      gemini_flash_casual_wins: 16\n      judges_significant_count: 3\n      judges_total: 3\n      cross_judge_winrate_range: [0.64, 0.72]\n      cross_judge_mean_winrate: 0.684\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality bias 是 LLM judge 的通用现象而非 GPT-4o 特有，因为 RLHF 训练数据普遍偏向\n      formal/professional 风格的回答——这是 preference data 的系统性采样偏差。Claude-Sonnet 效应\n      略弱（0.64 vs GPT-4o 0.69），因为 Anthropic 的 RLHF 流程有更多 helpfulness 导向的校准，\n      对 surface style 的依赖稍低；但 formal premium 仍然显著，因为底层 pretraining 数据中\n      formal text 与 higher-quality content 高度相关。Gemini-Flash 效应略强（0.72），因为\n      轻量模型更依赖 surface heuristics（style proxy）来做判断，formal tone 作为 quality\n      shortcut 的权重更大。三个 judge 全部显著（p<0.05）支持 A1 假设。效应量级差异\n      （0.64-0.72）同时支持 C3——bias 的 magnitude 是 judge-dependent 的。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: Formality Pairwise Results Across Judges (LLMBar, n=100)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal Wins\", \"Casual Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"95% CI\", \"Sign Test p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 55, 38, 17, \"69.1%\", \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\", \"0.006**\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 50, 32, 18, \"64.0%\", \"[50.1%, 75.9%]\", \"0.028*\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 58, 42, 16, \"72.4%\", \"[59.8%, 82.3%]\", \"0.002**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: 三个 judge 的 formal win rate 森林图（forest plot），每个 judge 一行，显示 point estimate + 95% Wilson CI。所有三个 CI 不跨 0.5 baseline，视觉上清晰展示 formality premium 的 cross-judge 一致性。\"\n      - \"Figure 3: Direction asymmetry grouped bar chart——每个 judge 分 formal→casual orig 和 casual→formal orig 两组，展示 win rate 差异。GPT-4o 不对称最大（~0.24 gap），Claude 最小（~0.10 gap）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      三个 judge 全部显著复现 formality bias，A1 假设成立。效应量级在 0.64-0.72 范围内，\n      跨 judge 一致但有量级差异——这是 C3（axis-dependency）的 judge 维度证据。\n      Gemini-Flash 最强可能反映轻量模型对 surface cues 更敏感。\n      方向不对称在所有 judge 上存在但程度不同：GPT-4o 最大（formal←casual orig 方向更强），\n      Claude 最对称——这为 exp-005 original preference 控制提供了动机。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 CSD 流程。需要新的 counterfactual generation\n      （不同 source text）。三个 judge（GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash）分别评测。\n      每个 benchmark n=100。与 LLMBar 结果交叉比较，形成 3×3 矩阵。\n    expected_results:\n      # AlpacaEval results\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.67\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_p: 0.012\n      alpacaeval_claude_formal_winrate: 0.61\n      alpacaeval_claude_p: 0.048\n      alpacaeval_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.70\n      alpacaeval_gemini_p: 0.004\n      alpacaeval_counterfactual_nli_pass: 0.90\n      # MT-Bench results\n      mtbench_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.65\n      mtbench_gpt4o_p: 0.018\n      mtbench_claude_formal_winrate: 0.60\n      mtbench_claude_p: 0.065\n      mtbench_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.68\n      mtbench_gemini_p: 0.008\n      mtbench_counterfactual_nli_pass: 0.87\n      # Cross-benchmark summary\n      significant_combos_total: 7\n      total_combos: 9\n      non_significant_combos: [\"Claude×MT-Bench (p=0.065)\",\"(borderline)\"]\n      mean_winrate_across_all: 0.668\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality bias 跨 benchmark 泛化，因为 bias 源于 judge 的内在偏好而非特定数据集的特征。\n      AlpacaEval 效应略强于 MT-Bench：AlpacaEval 的 open-ended instruction-following 任务\n      给 style variation 更大空间，formal tone 作为 quality proxy 的作用更明显；MT-Bench\n      的 multi-turn 结构和更 specific 的评判标准（如 math/reasoning accuracy）部分抑制了\n      style 的影响。Claude×MT-Bench 是唯一 borderline 不显著的组合（p=0.065），因为\n      Claude 在 MT-Bench 这种有明确正确性标准的 benchmark 上更倾向 content-based 判断。\n      但 7/9 组合显著（含 LLMBar 数据）远超偶然水平，A2 假设成立。\n      NLI pass rate 在 AlpacaEval (0.90) 略高于 MT-Bench (0.87)，因为 AlpacaEval 的\n      response 结构更简单，counterfactual 改写更容易保持语义。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: Formality Pairwise Win Rate Matrix (Judge × Benchmark)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"LLMBar\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"MT-Bench\", \"Mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"69.1%**\", \"67.0%*\", \"65.0%*\", \"67.0%\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", \"64.0%*\", \"61.0%*\", \"60.0%†\", \"61.7%\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", \"72.4%**\", \"70.0%**\", \"68.0%**\", \"70.1%\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"68.5%\", \"66.0%\", \"64.3%\", \"66.3%\"]\n        footnote: \"** p<0.01, * p<0.05, † p<0.10. n=100 per cell (n_consistent varies).\"\n      - title: \"Table 4: Counterfactual Quality per Benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"n\", \"NLI Pass Rate\", \"NLI Mean\", \"BERTScore Mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", 100, \"88%\", 0.896, 0.842]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", 100, \"90%\", 0.908, 0.851]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", 100, \"87%\", 0.882, 0.835]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 4: 3×3 heatmap，行为 judge，列为 benchmark，颜色深度表示 formal win rate（0.5-0.8 色标），每格标注 win rate 和显著性星号。视觉上一目了然：整个矩阵偏暖色，Gemini 行最深，MT-Bench 列最浅。\"\n      - \"Figure 5: Benchmark 间 effect size 比较——三个 benchmark 的 win rate 分布 boxplot，展示 LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench 的梯度。\"\n    analysis: >\n      9 个 judge×benchmark 组合中 7 个显著（p<0.05），剩余 1 个 borderline（Claude×MT-Bench p=0.065），\n      仅 0 个完全不显著。这远超 A2 要求的 5-9 个显著组合的下限。\n      Benchmark 梯度（LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench）有方法论意义：task-specific evaluation criteria\n      越强，style bias 越被抑制——这为 \"style bias 在 open-ended evaluation 中危害最大\" 的论点提供证据。\n      Judge 梯度（Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude）稳定跨 benchmark，说明 judge 的 style sensitivity\n      是其内在属性。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对 exp-001 和 exp-002 的每个 judge×benchmark 组合，计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate，\n      系统性比较两种 measurement 的 sensitivity。使用同一 counterfactual 数据。\n    expected_results:\n      # LLMBar\n      llmbar_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.10\n      llmbar_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.332\n      llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_winrate: 0.691\n      llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      llmbar_gpt4o_gap: true\n      llmbar_claude_likert_ate: 0.06\n      llmbar_claude_likert_p: 0.485\n      llmbar_claude_pairwise_winrate: 0.640\n      llmbar_claude_pairwise_p: 0.028\n      llmbar_claude_gap: true\n      llmbar_gemini_likert_ate: 0.14\n      llmbar_gemini_likert_p: 0.198\n      llmbar_gemini_pairwise_winrate: 0.724\n      llmbar_gemini_pairwise_p: 0.002\n      llmbar_gemini_gap: true\n      # AlpacaEval\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.08\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.412\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_pairwise_p: 0.012\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_gap: true\n      alpacaeval_claude_likert_p: 0.551\n      alpacaeval_claude_pairwise_p: 0.048\n      alpacaeval_claude_gap: true\n      alpacaeval_gemini_likert_p: 0.142\n      alpacaeval_gemini_pairwise_p: 0.004\n      alpacaeval_gemini_gap: true\n      # MT-Bench\n      mtbench_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.388\n      mtbench_gpt4o_pairwise_p: 0.018\n      mtbench_gpt4o_gap: true\n      mtbench_claude_likert_p: 0.612\n      mtbench_claude_pairwise_p: 0.065\n      mtbench_claude_gap: false\n      mtbench_gemini_likert_p: 0.175\n      mtbench_gemini_pairwise_p: 0.008\n      mtbench_gemini_gap: true\n      # Summary\n      gap_prevalence: 0.78\n      combos_with_gap: 7\n      combos_without_gap: 2\n      combos_total: 9\n      note: \"两个无 gap 的组合：Claude×MT-Bench（两者都不显著），因此不算 gap（一致性 non-significant）\"\n      mean_likert_p: 0.37\n      mean_pairwise_p: 0.021\n    result_rationale: >\n      Likert-Pairwise gap 的根因是 measurement scale 的信息结构差异。Likert pointwise 评分中，\n      style bias 被 (1) score anchoring（judge 倾向使用量表中段）、(2) absolute calibration noise\n      （不同 item 的 baseline quality 不同）、(3) within-subject variance 稀释。Pairwise 直接\n      呈现 A/B 对比，消除了 absolute calibration 问题，将 style 差异放大为 forced choice 中的\n      tie-breaking signal。在 best 档位，7/9 组合出现 gap（Likert 不显著但 Pairwise 显著），\n      gap prevalence 0.78 在 [0.67, 1.0] 范围内。唯一无 gap 的是 Claude×MT-Bench（两者都\n      不显著——pairwise 也仅 borderline p=0.065），这不违反 C2 因为 C2 的 claim 是 Likert\n      \"低估\" 而非 \"永远 miss\"：当 pairwise 也 miss 时，说明该组合的 true effect 本身很弱。\n      没有任何组合出现 Likert 显著但 Pairwise 不显著的 reverse pattern，强力支持 pairwise\n      严格更敏感的结论。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate — Systematic Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Judge × Benchmark\", \"Likert ATE\", \"Likert p\", \"Pairwise WR\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Gap?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar\", \"+0.10\", \"0.332\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar\", \"+0.06\", \"0.485\", \"64.0%\", \"0.028*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar\", \"+0.14\", \"0.198\", \"72.4%\", \"0.002**\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.08\", \"0.412\", \"67.0%\", \"0.012*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Claude × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.04\", \"0.551\", \"61.0%\", \"0.048*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.12\", \"0.142\", \"70.0%\", \"0.004**\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × MT-Bench\", \"+0.09\", \"0.388\", \"65.0%\", \"0.018*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Claude × MT-Bench\", \"+0.03\", \"0.612\", \"60.0%\", \"0.065†\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × MT-Bench\", \"+0.11\", \"0.175\", \"68.0%\", \"0.008**\", \"✓\"]\n        footnote: \"Gap = Likert p>0.10 AND Pairwise p<0.05. † borderline.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 6 (论文核心图): Paired dot plot——每个 judge×benchmark 组合一对点（Likert p 和 Pairwise p），用线段连接。Horizontal line 标注 α=0.05。几乎所有 Likert 点在线上方，Pairwise 点在线下方，视觉冲击力极强，直观展示 measurement gap。\"\n      - \"Figure 7: Likert score 分布 violin plot（formal vs casual），展示 why Likert fails——分布高度重叠，mean difference 被 variance 淹没。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 是本文最强 contribution。7/9 组合出现系统性 measurement gap，且无 reverse pattern。\n      这意味着现有文献中使用 Likert pointwise 方法研究 style bias 的工作（如基于 Likert 的\n      debiasing）可能系统性低估问题的严重程度。实践建议明确：style bias audit 应使用\n      pairwise comparison 而非 pointwise scoring。这个 insight 对 LLM-as-judge 社区\n      有直接、广泛的实用价值——是最强 reviewer hook。\n\n  - name: \"Tone axis (assertive/hedging) counterfactual + pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      测试 tone（assertive vs hedging）作为第二个工作维度。Full pipeline：counterfactual\n      generation → NLI content verification → pairwise scoring（dual-direction）→ ATE 分析。\n      三个 judge（GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash）× LLMBar。n=100。\n    expected_results:\n      # Content verification\n      tone_nli_pass_rate: 0.89\n      tone_nli_mean: 0.912\n      tone_bertscore_mean: 0.858\n      tone_both_pass: 0.86\n      # GPT-4o pairwise\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 52\n      gpt4o_assertive_wins: 33\n      gpt4o_hedging_wins: 19\n      gpt4o_assertive_win_rate: 0.635\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.038\n      # Claude pairwise\n      claude_n_consistent: 48\n      claude_assertive_wins: 28\n      claude_hedging_wins: 20\n      claude_assertive_win_rate: 0.583\n      claude_sign_test_p: 0.085\n      # Gemini pairwise\n      gemini_n_consistent: 54\n      gemini_assertive_wins: 37\n      gemini_hedging_wins: 17\n      gemini_assertive_win_rate: 0.685\n      gemini_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      # Cross-judge summary\n      judges_significant: 2\n      judges_total: 3\n      mean_assertive_winrate: 0.634\n      # Likert comparison (for C2)\n      gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.07\n      gpt4o_likert_p: 0.448\n      claude_likert_p: 0.621\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.231\n      tone_likert_pairwise_gap: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Tone axis 成功开辟第二维度，因为 assertive/hedging 改写在语义保持上与 formality 类似——\n      改变表达的确信程度（confidence markers, hedging phrases）而不改变信息内容，NLI pass 0.89\n      在 [0.85, 0.93] 范围内。Assertive tone 产生 premium 的机制与 formality 平行但不同：\n      LLM judge 在 RLHF 中学到 \"confident = competent\" 的 heuristic，assertive 回答被\n      associative 地认为更 knowledgeable。效应略弱于 formality（mean 0.634 vs 0.684），\n      因为 tone 是更微妙的 surface cue——formality 涉及词汇和句法层面的系统性变化，\n      而 tone 主要体现在 hedging markers 和 modal verbs 上，judge 的 sensitivity 更低。\n      Claude 在 tone 上 borderline 不显著（p=0.085），因为 Anthropic 训练中可能有更多\n      关于 epistemic humility 的 alignment，对 hedging 的 penalty 较小。Gemini 仍然最强\n      （0.685），进一步确认轻量模型对 surface cues 更 sensitive。两个 judge 显著 + 一个\n      borderline 足以支持 C1 和 C3 在 tone axis 上的 claim。A3 和 A4 假设成立。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 6: Tone Axis Content Verification\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"n\", 100]\n          - [\"NLI Pass Rate (≥0.85)\", \"89%\"]\n          - [\"NLI Mean\", 0.912]\n          - [\"BERTScore Mean\", 0.858]\n          - [\"Both Pass Rate\", \"86%\"]\n      - title: \"Table 7: Tone (Assertive vs Hedging) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Assert. Wins\", \"Hedge Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"95% CI\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 52, 33, 19, \"63.5%\", \"[49.9%, 75.2%]\", \"0.038*\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 48, 28, 20, \"58.3%\", \"[44.3%, 71.1%]\", \"0.085†\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 54, 37, 17, \"68.5%\", \"[55.4%, 79.3%]\", \"0.006**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 8: 双 axis 效应比较——grouped bar chart，x 轴为 judge，每个 judge 两根 bar（formality win rate 和 tone win rate），展示 axis-dependency。Formality bar 系统性高于 tone bar，但两者都在 50% 以上。\"\n      - \"Figure 9: Tone counterfactual 示例对比——展示 2-3 个 assertive/hedging pair，标注 NLI score，帮助读者理解改写质量。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Tone axis 成功验证 CSD 框架的 multi-axis 能力。两个 axis 效应模式不同\n      （formality 更强且跨 judge 一致，tone 略弱且 Claude 上 borderline），\n      直接支持 C3——style bias 是 axis-dependent 的，不能把 \"style\" 当单一维度。\n      Tone 的 Likert 同样全部不显著，进一步扩展 C2 的 evidence。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Original text vs 同风格 double-rewrite 的 pairwise 比较。量化 original preference\n      confound。如果 win rate ≈50%，original preference 可忽略，style 是主要驱动力。\n      GPT-4o × LLMBar，n=100。\n    expected_results:\n      n_valid: 95\n      n_consistent: 60\n      original_wins: 32\n      rewrite_wins: 28\n      original_win_rate: 0.533\n      sign_test_p: 0.362\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.408\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.655\n      position_bias_check: 0.52\n      # Subgroup analysis\n      formal_orig_original_winrate: 0.55\n      casual_orig_original_winrate: 0.52\n      nli_ge90_original_winrate: 0.51\n    result_rationale: >\n      Original preference 可忽略（win rate 0.533 在 [0.47, 0.53] 范围边缘，p=0.362 远不显著），\n      因为 double-rewrite 过程虽然引入了轻微的 \"rewrite artifact\"（如稍微不自然的措辞），\n      但这个 artifact 对 judge 的影响是随机的而非系统性的。Win rate 略偏向 original（53.3%\n      而非精确 50%），反映了 rewrite 过程确实有微小的 quality degradation，但量级远小于\n      formality 的 69.1% 或 tone 的 63.5%。这意味着 exp-001/002/004 中观察到的 style\n      premium 主要由 style 本身驱动，而非 \"original 比 rewrite 更自然\" 的 confound。\n      方向不对称（MVP 中 formal←casual orig 0.79 vs casual←formal orig 0.55）的主要解释\n      从 \"original preference\" 转向 \"改写方向的非对称难度\"：将 casual 改为 formal 更容易\n      保持质量，因此 formal←casual 方向的 counterfactual 质量更高，效应更强。\n      A6 假设成立：direction asymmetry 主要由 style 驱动，original preference 贡献 <5%。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 8: Original Preference Control (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"n (valid pairs)\", 95]\n          - [\"n (consistent)\", 60]\n          - [\"Original Wins\", 32]\n          - [\"Rewrite Wins\", 28]\n          - [\"Original Win Rate\", \"53.3%\"]\n          - [\"95% CI\", \"[40.8%, 65.5%]\"]\n          - [\"Sign Test p\", \"0.362\"]\n      - title: \"Table 9: Effect Size Decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"Win Rate\", \"p\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formality premium (CSD)\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"Style-driven causal effect\"]\n          - [\"Original preference\", \"53.3%\", \"0.362\", \"Negligible confound\"]\n          - [\"Corrected formality estimate\", \"~65.8%\", \"—\", \"Conservative lower bound\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 10: 三组 win rate 对比 bar chart——formality pairwise (69.1%), tone pairwise (63.5%), original preference control (53.3%)，各带 95% CI error bar。Original preference 的 CI 跨 50%，而 style axes 的 CI 不跨 50%。直观展示 style effect vs confound 的量级差异。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference confound 可安全忽略。53.3% 的微小偏移可解释 direction asymmetry\n      的一小部分（≤3-5 个百分点），但 formality 的 19.1% premium 和 tone 的 13.5% premium\n      远大于此。保守估计（扣除 original preference 后）formality 仍有 ~15.8% premium，\n      高度显著。这回应了 RC3 reviewer concern。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 formality pairwise 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=500。选择 exp-001/002 中效应最强的\n      judge×benchmark 组合（预期 Gemini×LLMBar）。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable\n      effect size。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 500\n      n_valid_both_trials: 490\n      n_consistent: 282\n      formal_wins: 192\n      casual_wins: 90\n      formal_win_rate: 0.681\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.624\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.733\n      sign_test_p: 0.0000003\n      cohens_h: 0.378\n      # Power analysis\n      power_at_n100_for_d065: 0.72\n      power_at_n300_for_d065: 0.97\n      power_at_n500_for_d065: 0.995\n      minimum_detectable_effect_n500: 0.56\n      # Subgroup stability\n      first_100_winrate: 0.70\n      second_100_winrate: 0.67\n      third_100_winrate: 0.69\n      fourth_100_winrate: 0.66\n      fifth_100_winrate: 0.70\n      subgroup_variance: 0.0003\n      # NLI stratification at scale\n      nli_ge90_n: 420\n      nli_ge90_winrate: 0.695\n      nli_ge80_n: 465\n      nli_ge80_winrate: 0.683\n    result_rationale: >\n      Scaled replication 在 n=500 时 win rate 0.681 在 [0.6, 0.72] 范围内，与 n=100\n      的 0.691 高度一致（仅 -1% regression to mean），说明 MVP 阶段的 point estimate\n      不是 small-sample 侥幸。CI 从 n=100 的 [0.56, 0.80] 收窄到 [0.62, 0.73]，\n      p 值从 0.006 降到 <0.001，sign_test_p 达到 3×10⁻⁷ 量级。五个 n=100 子组的\n      win rate 在 0.66-0.70 范围内波动极小（σ²=0.0003），展示效应的高度稳定性。\n      Power analysis 显示 n=100 对 d=0.065（Likert ATE 量级）只有 0.72 power——\n      这正好解释了为什么 Likert 在 n=100 时 miss：不是 Likert 完全无效，而是对弱信号\n      的 statistical power 不足。n=500 时 power 达 0.995，即使 Likert 也应 borderline\n      显著——但 pairwise 在 n=100 就能 catch，说明 pairwise 的 effective sample size\n      更大（每对 within-subject 对比消除了 item-level variance）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 10: Scaled Replication — Formality Pairwise (Gemini × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Scale\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal WR\", \"95% CI\", \"p\", \"Cohen's h\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"n=100 (MVP)\", 55, \"69.1%\", \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\", \"0.006\", \"0.393\"]\n          - [\"n=100 (sub1)\", 58, \"70.0%\", \"[57.3%, 80.4%]\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"n=100 (sub2)\", 54, \"67.0%\", \"[53.7%, 78.1%]\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"n=100 (sub3)\", 56, \"69.0%\", \"[56.1%, 79.6%]\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"n=100 (sub4)\", 55, \"66.0%\", \"[52.9%, 77.1%]\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"n=100 (sub5)\", 59, \"70.0%\", \"[57.5%, 80.2%]\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"n=500 (full)\", 282, \"68.1%\", \"[62.4%, 73.3%]\", \"<0.001\", \"0.378\"]\n      - title: \"Table 11: Power Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"n\", \"Power (d=0.065)\", \"Power (d=0.18)\", \"Min Detectable WR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [100, \"0.72\", \"0.99\", \"62.0%\"]\n          - [300, \"0.97\", \">0.999\", \"57.5%\"]\n          - [500, \"0.995\", \">0.999\", \"56.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 11: Cumulative win rate plot——x 轴为 sample size (50→500)，y 轴为 cumulative formal win rate，带 running 95% CI band。Win rate 从早期波动逐渐收敛到 ~0.68，CI band 稳定收窄。\"\n      - \"Figure 12: Power curve——x 轴为 n，y 轴为 power，三条线分别对应 d=0.065 (Likert ATE), d=0.18 (pairwise effect), d=0.10 (intermediate)。标注 n=100 和 n=500 的 power 值。直观展示 Likert 在 n=100 power 不足的原因。\"\n    analysis: >\n      n=500 replication 是对 RC5 (sample size) 的决定性回应。效应稳定、CI 收窄、\n      p 值极小。Power analysis 同时为 C2 提供了额外解释——Likert 的 measurement gap\n      部分来自 power 不足（pointwise 的 between-item variance 稀释了 weak signal），\n      而 pairwise 的 within-subject design 在 n=100 就有足够 power。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      第三个 surface-level axis。Academic vs conversational register 改变词汇和句法\n      但不改变信息内容。Full pipeline：counterfactual gen → content verification →\n      pairwise scoring。三个 judge × LLMBar，n=100。\n    expected_results:\n      # Content verification\n      register_nli_pass_rate: 0.86\n      register_nli_mean: 0.893\n      register_bertscore_mean: 0.839\n      # Pairwise results\n      gpt4o_academic_win_rate: 0.66\n      gpt4o_p: 0.015\n      claude_academic_win_rate: 0.62\n      claude_p: 0.042\n      gemini_academic_win_rate: 0.71\n      gemini_p: 0.003\n      judges_significant: 3\n      mean_academic_winrate: 0.663\n      # Likert gap\n      gpt4o_likert_p: 0.289\n      claude_likert_p: 0.511\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.167\n      register_likert_pairwise_gap: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Register axis 效应在 formality 和 tone 之间（mean 0.663），因为 academic/conversational\n      register 的改变涉及词汇层面（Latinate vs Germanic words, disciplinary jargon vs\n      everyday terms）和句法层面（复杂从句 vs 简单句），比 tone 更 salient 但比 formality\n      更窄（formality 包含 register + tone + other cues 的 composite）。NLI pass rate 0.86\n      略低于 formality (0.88) 和 tone (0.89)，因为 academic register 中的 disciplinary\n      vocabulary 有时会引入微妙的语义偏移（如用术语替代 layman terms 可能 shift specificity），\n      但仍在 [0.85, 0.93] 范围内。三个 judge 全部显著，进一步证明 CSD 框架的通用性。\n      现在有 3 working axes + 1 failing axis (verbosity)，C3 的 evidence 非常充分。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 12: Register (Academic vs Conversational) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Academic Wins\", \"Conversational Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 53, 35, 18, \"66.0%\", \"0.015*\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 50, 31, 19, \"62.0%\", \"0.042*\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 56, 40, 16, \"71.4%\", \"0.003**\"]\n      - title: \"Table 13: Cross-Axis Summary (all on LLMBar, 3 judges)\"\n        columns: [\"Axis\", \"Mean WR\", \"Judges Sig.\", \"NLI Pass\", \"Likert Detects?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formality\", \"68.4%\", \"3/3\", \"88%\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"Register\", \"66.3%\", \"3/3\", \"86%\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"Tone\", \"63.4%\", \"2/3\", \"89%\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"Verbosity\", \"—\", \"—\", \"65%\", \"N/A (failed H1)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 13: 四 axis 汇总——每个 axis 一行 forest plot，formal/register/tone 都有显著 CI 不跨 0.5，verbosity 标注为 method boundary (NLI fail)。一图讲完整个 C3 story。\"\n    analysis: >\n      三个 working axes 构成强有力的 C3 evidence：style bias 是 axis-dependent 的，\n      且效应量级系统性排序（formality > register > tone）。这不是偶然——效应强度与\n      改写涉及的 linguistic level 数量正相关（formality 跨词汇+句法+语用，register 跨词汇+句法，\n      tone 主要在语用层）。Verbosity 作为第四个 axis 的失败提供了 principled boundary：\n      改变信息量的 axis 违反内容保持假设，是方法论限制而非方法失败。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为替代 rewriter，对 LLMBar formality 运行完整 pipeline。\n      与 Qwen3-32B 结果比较，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n    expected_results:\n      # Content verification comparison\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      llama_nli_mean: 0.881\n      llama_bertscore_mean: 0.836\n      qwen_nli_pass_rate: 0.88\n      qwen_nli_mean: 0.896\n      # Pairwise comparison (GPT-4o judge)\n      llama_formal_win_rate: 0.66\n      llama_sign_test_p: 0.015\n      qwen_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n      qwen_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      # Statistical comparison\n      winrate_difference: 0.031\n      fisher_exact_p_difference: 0.42\n      rewriter_effect_significant: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama rewriter 产生略低但仍显著的 formality premium（0.66 vs Qwen 0.69），\n      差异不显著（Fisher p=0.42）。Llama NLI pass rate 略低（0.85 vs 0.88），\n      因为 Llama-70B 在 instruction following 上略弱于 Qwen3-32B（后者受益于 Qwen3\n      的强 instruction tuning），导致少量 counterfactual 有轻微语义偏移。但关键结论\n      不变：formality bias 的检测不依赖于特定 rewriter family。3% 的 win rate 差异\n      在统计噪声范围内，可能反映 counterfactual quality 的微小差异而非系统性 artifact。\n      这排除了 \"Qwen rewriter 引入了某种被 judge 偏好的 writing pattern\" 的 confound。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 14: Rewriter Ablation (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality)\"\n        columns: [\"Rewriter\", \"NLI Pass\", \"NLI Mean\", \"Formal WR\", \"p\", \"n_consistent\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"88%\", 0.896, \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", 55]\n          - [\"Llama-3.1-70B\", \"85%\", 0.881, \"66.0%\", \"0.015*\", 52]\n          - [\"Difference\", \"-3%\", \"-0.015\", \"-3.1%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Fisher exact (diff)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"p=0.42\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure A1 (appendix): Side-by-side counterfactual 质量对比——Qwen vs Llama 的 NLI score 分布 histogram，分布形状相似，Llama 略左偏。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter ablation 确认 CSD 结果的 robustness。这是 appendix 级实验而非 main text，\n      但对 reviewer 质疑 rewriter choice 时提供决定性回应。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"716ef52e-c7c5-4277-86fe-b34ea8047dee","total_cost_usd":0.403167,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11418,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"output_tokens":12800,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11418,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12800,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11418,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11418},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5971,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006071,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12800,"cacheReadInputTokens":11447,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11418,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.397096,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"2d83c896-8810-4bd9-bb0e-3683ad315a7f"}
